From c05f9facc427e45d7ff621b52602c335e3a6ed0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:03:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Render: the shaders' text compacted, identical GLSL

The index chunk stood at 2643.7 of its 2645 kB ceiling, and the offset
budgets.json names for it is the text of the /* glsl */ template strings,
whose comments and indentation ship verbatim. Before the sky work adds
shader code (owner's answer 7 of 2026-10-17):

- The comments inside the GLSL of entry-glow, orbit-view, plume, smoke,
  stars, trails and vapour move, word for word, into JS comments above
  each shader const (scene.ts's were moved in d8fe18f).
- Every line inside the 32 /* glsl */ templates of src/render loses its
  leading indentation, scene.ts's four included.

Identical output: each changed file was parsed (oxc, via rolldown's
parseAst) at 23cb4cf and here, and the ASTs compared without positions,
with every glsl template's text replaced by its GLSL token stream
(comments dropped, whitespace collapsed, the end of each preprocessor
line kept as a token, whitespace at a ${} boundary kept): 11 files, 32
shaders, 7878 GLSL tokens, identical. The check fails on a changed
number and on a #include joined to the next line (negative controls).
A harness rendering SceneManager with the app's Earth textures in
headless Chromium (SwiftShader) gives pixel-identical frames at 23cb4cf
and here on 8 views (400 km limb and terminator, nadir, 30 km, 12 km,
the pad at dusk twice, the gradient sky).

Measured index 2638.9 kB (2643.7 before; 4.8 kB saved), no ceiling
touched. tsc clean; the 23 render test files pass (261 tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
